# CubeOS Roadmap

## v0.2 - World Generation Update
- Terrain generation:
  - Add mountains (multi-noise heightmap with sharper peaks).
  - Add caves (3D noise carve pass).
  - Add canyons (erosion/ridge mask + depth carve).
- Nature:
  - Add tree generation (trunk + leaves templates, biome-aware spawn rules).
- Blocks and resources:
  - Add water block (source + flowing behavior, basic propagation limits).
  - Add ores (coal, iron, gold) with height-based spawn distribution.
  - Add additional terrain blocks (sand, gravel, wood, leaves).
- Inventory at game start:
  - Remove pre-filled hotbar/inventory.
  - Start with empty inventory by default.

Definition of done:
- New world visibly includes mountains, caves, canyons, trees, water and ores.
- New game starts with empty inventory and empty hotbar.

## v0.2.0-v0.2.2 - Main Menu & World Setup
- Main menu:
  - Add title screen with `Start`, `Settings`, `Quit`.
  - Add background scene and basic UI transitions.
- Start flow:
  - Add `Create World` screen before entering game.
  - World name input and seed input.
- World presets:
  - `Classic Flat` (current flat-style preset).
  - `Minecraft-style` (varied terrain with mountains/valleys/ravines).
- World settings (v0.2 scope):
  - Preset selection.
  - Generate structures toggle (prepared for future).
  - Cave density slider.
  - Ravine frequency slider.
  - Starting inventory mode (`Empty` / `Creative test`).
- Save settings:
  - Store selected preset and generation settings in world metadata.
  - Use settings when generating new chunks for that world.

Definition of done:
- Player enters the game only through main menu/create-world flow.
- Player can create worlds with at least `Classic Flat` and `Minecraft-style` presets.
- Chosen settings are saved and restored per world.

## v0.2.3 - Coins & Upgrade Progression
- Coin gameplay loop:
  - Spawn collectible coins across generated world areas.
  - Add pickup feedback (sound/UI counter) and persistent coin balance.
  - Prevent immediate respawn farming around player spawn.
- Main menu upgrades:
  - Add `Upgrades` screen in main menu.
  - Spend coins on character upgrades.
  - First upgrade set: underwater hold-breath duration.
- Upgrade system:
  - Define upgrade levels, price curve, and max level caps.
  - Save/load purchased upgrades per world profile.
- Balance pass:
  - Tune coin spawn density and upgrade prices for early progression.

Definition of done:
- Player can collect coins in world and keep balance between sessions.
- Player can buy at least one upgrade in main menu and feel effect in gameplay.

## v0.3.0 - Tools, Mining & Render Streaming Parity
- Add tools:
  - Wooden, stone and iron pickaxe.
  - Axe and shovel (same material tiers).
- Tool behavior:
  - Mining speed modifiers by tool type/material.
  - Correct block effectiveness (pickaxe for stone/ore, axe for wood, shovel for dirt/sand).
  - Durability and break mechanics.
- Resource drops:
  - Ores drop proper items only with correct tool tier.
- UI:
  - Tool icons and durability display in hotbar/inventory.
- Rendering architecture (Minecraft-style parity):
  - Full render-layer split (`solid` / `cutout` / `translucent`) with dedicated transparent sorting.
  - More aggressive section culling (frustum + occlusion).
  - More mature GPU sync and upload batching pipeline for chunk-section streaming.

Definition of done:
- Player can craft/use tools (or obtain them in test mode) and mine faster with proper tool.
- Durability decreases and tools break correctly.
- Moving across chunk borders does not cause noticeable frame spikes from mesh rebuild/upload bursts.

## v0.4 - Balance & Polish
- Balance world parameters:
  - Ore rates and depth ranges.
  - Tree density.
  - Water spread limits and performance impact.
- Improve generation stability:
  - Reduce chunk seams/artifacts in caves and canyons.
- Gameplay polish:
  - Tune break time, drop rates, and early-game progression.

Definition of done:
- Stable world generation without obvious seams.
- Early survival loop feels consistent and playable.
